{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789333102,"nonce":"gS0uAfDX8vvorKxXhfWtcPUwQU4=","title":"Dynamic box reads are extern calls the optimizer cannot see through","message":"Every read out of a dynamic box in the builtins library is an extern call\ninto the runtime: `zb_box_tag` (`zyntax_box_get_tag`), `zb_box_get_i64`,\n`zb_box_get_f64`, `zb_box_get_bool`, and the `data` pointer readers\n`zb_unbox_list_raw_*`, `zb_unbox_instance_raw`, `zb_box_get_str`\n(`zyntax_box_get_opaque`). Each is a load or two behind a call: the box is\n`{ tag: u32, size: u32, data: *u8, dropper, display }` and the payload sits\nbehind `data`.\n\nBecause they are calls to externs, the compiler treats them as impure:\nLICM hoists none of them and no load past them, CSE does not merge two\nreads of the same box, DCE keeps one whose result is unused, and purity\ninference marks every function that reads a box impure, which blocks\npure-call PRE for the recursion around it.\n\nWhere it shows, after 86da450 (10M iterations, Cranelift tier):\n\n    bench_lambda_call.py    zypy 19.5 ms   zynml 13.2 ms\n        loop body: one dead `zb_unbox_list_raw_any(record)` (the typed\n        entry ignores `env` when nothing is captured) plus the pending\n        check.\n    bench_closure_call.py   zypy 67.7 ms\n        loop body: `zb_unbox_list_raw_any(record)`, a load, then\n        `zb_unbox_list_raw_any(cell)`, a load, `zyntax_box_get_i64`,\n        all loop-invariant, none hoistable.\n\nFix: declare the box as a `@reference` struct type in the builtins\nlibrary, matching `sdk/zrtl/src/dynamic_box.rs`, and define the readers\nas field reads through it: `tag` and `data` as fields, the scalar payloads\nas a field read through `data` cast to a one-field struct of the payload\ntype. A null box keeps the extern's result (VOID tag, null, 0) through a\nselect. The readers then lower to gep and load on every backend, and the\nloads above hoist, merge and die like any other. `zb_box_get_i64`'s width\nswitch on `size` is only needed where a box of another width can reach;\nthe checked readers already know the tag, so the I64 arm reads eight bytes\nand the BOOL arm one.\n\nCheck on all four backends, with the box layout pinned by a test against\nthe runtime's own constructors.","files":null}]}